Functional Requirements

1. A Web-Based Application (Main Application)
A working HTML/CSS website that runs in a web browser
Key Information:
Uses HTML & CSS 
Connects to two SQL databases
Automatically opens to Page 1 when launched
Contains 25 total pages

2. Two Searchable SQL Databases
You must design and implement two separate databases:
Key Information:
Database 1: Staff
Stores information about staff who worked at the school, e.g.:
Staff ID
Name
Role
Dates of employment

Database 2: Sources
Stores information about historical sources, e.g.:
Source ID
Title
Type (book, document, image, logbook, etc.)
Location
Linked image/page reference
Both databases must be searchable via the website (search forms or filters).


3. Hyperlinked Images Folder
Create an Images folder that:
Links to text and table entries in the pages
Subdivided into folders
Some text and page numbers inside tables must link to the correct image or document.

4. 25 Interlinked Pages
Your site must include:
25 HTML pages total
Proper navigation (menus, buttons, links)
Consistent layout/design across pages
Page 1 as the landing page

5. Reusable Design
After the site works:
The headers must be able to be modified so the design can be reused for other projects
Titles
Logos
Navigation labels
This should be explained within the instruction manual detailing how to change them

6. Clean, Documented Code
Every HTML and CSS file must:
Be clearly commented, explaining:
What each section does
What can be changed and not changed!


7. Clear Instruction Manual
A separate instruction manual which should include:
How the system works
Where the databases are stored
How to:
Modify headers for new projects
Change text/images safely
Add new staff or sources
Which parts of the code:
Are safe to edit
Must not be altered
How images and folders are structured


Constraints
 
1. Time
Limited development time
Developing 25 pages, 2 databases and documentation is time consuming so:
Pages may need reused templates 
Features must stay simple but functional
Testing and debugging time wil also be limited 

2. Technical Skills
HTML and CSS only for the interface 
Basic SQL (SELECT, INSERT, simple WHERE clauses) 
Searches may be basic (keyword search, drop-down filters) 

3. Usability
Target users are researchers and historians  
Interface must be easy to navigate
Interface must be clearly labelled 
Interface must be searchable without training 

4. Software and environment 
Must be running locally on XAMPP/Localhost
Browser – based access only 
Limited or field database software (MySQL)  

5. Data
Historical records may be incomplete, inconsistent and sensitive
Clearly labelled sample records
Personal data must be handled carefully

